oversight passage.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},{"reason":"Preserves post-vetting and possible regulatory follow-up despite prior-approval relief.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},{"reason":"Provides a clarification route without adding a substantive approval condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},{"reason":"Signatory division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing body.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},{"reason":"Defines the covered UCITS population by domicile and status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"reason":"FAQ reference only; linked substantive requirements cannot be determined from this packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},{"reason":"Forms and checklists reference only; linked contents cannot be determined from this packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control concerns material investment changes in the post-authorisation setting for the circular's defined UCITS funds. Management companies are addressed, but the relief attaches to scheme changes. Other funds and operator changes are outside this selected control.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u11.2030","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"UCITS funds is expressly defined. Materiality, novel or complex product features, home-jurisdiction compliance and possible local policy implications lack operational definitions in the supplied text.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The exceptions attach to approval relief for investment changes: novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications independently defeats the stated relief. The language does not support requiring all three together.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The text removes a prior-approval requirement for qualifying changes. It does not certify compliance or eliminate notification, filing, post-vetting or regulatory action. Failure to qualify for removal does not itself fully establish the underlying approval obligation.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The express date is 28 November 2025. Pre-date applications pending at transition retain existing processing. Whether this necessarily preserves a substantive prior-approval prerequisite, rather than just the handling of the application, is not fully specified.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The operative FAQs, referenced forms and checklists, home requirements and existing approval process are not supplied. The two dependency records have no source hashes or contents, and cannot be reliably mapped to particular referenced documents.","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What do the operative FAQs say about materiality, novelty, complexity and possible local policy implications?","Does retaining the existing approval process for a pending pre-Effective-Date application also preserve the substantive prerequisite of approval before implementation, and may the application be withdrawn to use the new measures?","Do the FAQs impose any separate home-supervision condition beyond compliance with home-jurisdiction requirements for investment changes?","What underlying approval rules apply where this circular's removal does not apply?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The express Effective Date supplies the date intended by the introductory immediate-effect language.","The selected formal control excludes applications caught by the transition, because their treatment requires the existing process and missing FAQs.","The introductory reference to home supervision describes the measures' purpose; it is not treated as an additional independently specified condition in item (ii)."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"The text supports a clear removal-of-approval eligibility rule for changes outside the transition, rather than rival conjunctive and disjunctive exception rules. For example, an ordinary home-compliant investment-policy change in a covered Irish UCITS after the Effective Date qualifies if it has no possible local policy implications; the same change with possible local policy implications does not qualify even if it is neither novel nor complex. For an otherwise identical application received on 27 November 2025 and pending at transition, existing processing applies and this formal control gives no answer. The strongest uncertainty is whether that preserved processing also necessarily preserves the substantive approval prerequisite.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS, within the circular's definition.","name":"covered_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change is a post-authorisation material change to the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"covered_material_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The date as of which availability of the circular's approval removal is assessed; this does not select an implementation-date test for every transitional situation.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"An application concerning this change was received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 and remained without approval or authorisation at the Effective Date.","name":"pending_legacy_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed investment change complies with the fund's applicable home-jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves novel product features.","name":"novel_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves complex product features.","name":"complex_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required by this wording.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and home_requirements_met (not (or novel_features complex_features possible_local_policy_implications)))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_ucits covered_material_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) (not pending_legacy_application))"},"local_id":"approval_removal_eligibility","questions":["For a pending legacy application, does existing processing require approval before the change can take effect, or only govern disposition of the already-filed application?","What evidence and interpretive standards establish home compliance and the absence of each exception under the missing FAQs?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for a material UCITS investment change outside the legacy-application transition. Within the stated scope, true means the change meets the circular's stated home-compliance condition and none of its stated exceptions applies. False means this removal is unavailable under those conditions; it does not independently establish a prohibition, non-compliance or the complete underlying approval obligation. Outside scope, the result supplies no determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.","subject":"Prior-approval removal for material changes to UCITS investment objectives, policies or restrictions"}]},"run_id":"run.57127ace1fc14bbe97f783a02f719446"}